#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10133
msgid "CSS Bundling"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10134
msgid "Create local UltraCache CSS bundles for eligible stylesheet links. Safe mode is the public default. Aggressive and Full CSS Bundle are experimental and should be enabled only after visual testing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10141
msgid "CSS Bundling Scope"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10142
msgid "Choose exactly one scope for generated CSS bundles. Homepage only is safest, shared reuses the homepage bundle where possible, and per-page creates separate bundles for cacheable pages."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10147
msgid "Homepage only"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10148
msgid "Shared site bundle"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10149
msgid "Per-page bundles"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10153
msgid "CSS Bundle Mode"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10154
msgid "Choose how broadly UltraCache combines eligible local stylesheet links. Safe is recommended for public defaults; Aggressive and Full CSS Bundle are experimental and can increase blocking CSS or break layouts on some themes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10161
msgid "Full CSS Bundle"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10166
msgid "Inline CSS Bundling"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10167
msgid "Inline the generated page CSS bundle directly into the document head. This is user-controlled and can greatly increase cached HTML size when the generated bundle is large; STORE profiler now shows final HTML size, inline CSS bytes, and fallback counts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10174
msgid "Consolidate Remaining CSS"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10175
msgid "After the main CSS bundle is injected, combine eligible leftover non-protected local stylesheet links into one extra CSS file. SR7/Revolution/Swiper/Slick hero CSS remains protected; this targets small leftover plugin/theme CSS calls that still block rendering."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10182
msgid "First Visit CSS Bundle Handling"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10183
msgid "Choose what happens when a visitor opens a page before its CSS bundle exists."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10188
msgid "Do nothing"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10189
msgid "Build CSS bundle on entry"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10190
msgid "Build CSS bundle async"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10194
msgid "Async Remaining CSS"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10195
msgid "Rewrite low-risk local stylesheet links and UltraCache-generated external CSS bundles/optimized CSS to non-blocking print+onload loading with a noscript fallback. This complements CSS Bundling."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10202
msgid "Async external CSS"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10203
msgid "Converts stylesheet links from other domains to non-render-blocking async CSS. Same-site stylesheets continue through the normal CSS optimization/bundling flow."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10210
msgid "Aggressive Async CSS"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10211
msgid "Optional advanced mode. Rewrite almost all remaining local stylesheet links, including late footer output, to non-blocking print+onload loading with a noscript fallback. Use the exclude list for styles that must stay blocking."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10222
msgid "Fonts Optimization"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10223
msgid "Optimize remote Google Fonts, local @font-face display behavior, self-hosted font CSS delivery, and optional delayed icon-font loading."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10228
msgid "Font Display Optimization"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10229
msgid "Adds font-display: swap to local @font-face declarations when missing and appends display=swap to remote Google Fonts requests. Uses the existing Google Fonts Swap setting internally for backward compatibility."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10236
msgid "Local Google Fonts Optimization"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10237
msgid "Opt-in feature. Download Google Fonts CSS and WOFF2 files into the UltraCache cache, rewrite frontend Google Fonts links and Google Fonts @import rules found in loaded same-origin CSS, and keep font-display: swap on localized CSS. This feature makes outbound requests to Google Fonts when building the local cache."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10248
msgid "Optimize Self-Hosted Font CSS"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10249
msgid "Rewrite local and inline @font-face CSS to add font-display: swap, prefer matching WOFF2 sources when available, normalize font URLs, and preload up to two likely first-paint WOFF2 files."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10256
msgid "Bundle Generated Font-Mix CSS"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10257
msgid "Consolidate UltraCache-generated optimized-css/css-font-mix stylesheets into one ordered blocking CSS file. This reduces render-blocking request count without asyncing layout-risk CSS."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10261
msgid ""
"What it does: combines UltraCache-generated font-mix CSS files into one ordered stylesheet.\n"
"\n"
"Why it helps: the browser has one font CSS request to handle instead of many small blocking requests.\n"
"\n"
"Watch for: this bundle stays blocking on purpose because font CSS can change text size, icon display, and first-view layout."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10265
msgid "Async Generated Font-Mix CSS Bundle"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10266
msgid "Load the consolidated bundle-font-mix stylesheet with non-blocking print+onload delivery. Individual css-font-mix source files are not async-loaded by this option."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10270
msgid ""
"What it does: async-loads only the single consolidated bundle-font-mix stylesheet.\n"
"\n"
"Why it helps: a large font-mix bundle can leave the render-blocking path, so the page can paint sooner.\n"
"\n"
"Watch for: text or icons may appear with fallback styling first and settle later. Check the first viewport, product cards, menus, headers, and decorative fonts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10274
msgid "Delay icon fonts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10275
msgid "Moves only matching entries from the visible font pattern list into a non-render-blocking delayed font stylesheet. Use the scanner to append detected icon-font patterns, then save the visible list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10282
msgid "Advanced Runtime Font CSS Rewrite"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10283
msgid "Advanced opt-in / experimental. Uses a MutationObserver to rewrite late-injected local font stylesheet links. Keep off unless a site specifically needs runtime font-link rewriting."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10294
msgid "WooCommerce Controls"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10295
msgid "Control WooCommerce cache safety, frontend request timing, and optional asset cleanup."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10300
msgid "WooCommerce Safe Mode"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10301
msgid "Bypass cart, checkout, account, order endpoints, and cart-changing requests."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10310
msgid "WooCommerce frontend strategy"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10311
msgid "Choose a preset for cart-fragments timing and WooCommerce asset cleanup. Custom appears when the individual controls no longer match a preset."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10321
msgid ""
"What it does: applies a WooCommerce preset. Off disables UltraCache Woo timing and cleanup. Safe delays cart fragments only. Balanced also enables general Woo asset cleanup and removes Woo Blocks CSS when no Woo blocks are found. Aggressive adds product/gallery cleanup outside product pages and product-filter cleanup when no filter is found. Custom means the small switches no longer match a preset.\n"
"\n"
"Why it helps: WooCommerce often loads cart and shop helpers before the visitor needs them.\n"
"\n"
"Watch for: test homepage, shop, product, cart, checkout, account, mini-cart, add-to-cart, search, and filters after changing this."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10332
msgid "Cart fragments behavior"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-dashboard.js:10333
msgid "Choose whether WooCommerce cart fragments stay off, are delayed, or are suppressed on anonymous empty-cart cacheable pages. Cart, checkout, account, logged-in, and active cart/session-cookie contexts keep normal WooCommerce behavior."
msgstr ""

